      "summary": "Finance Minister Riikka Purra held a Finns Party event ('Acceleration Races') in Helsinki, sharply attacking SDP leader Antti Lindtman, unveiling a new dandelion party logo, calling for constitutional changes on immigration, and pledging no further welfare cuts while vowing strict immigration conditions for future coalitions. SDP reacted immediately, accusing Purra of factual distortions."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Government prepares emergency session on hantavirus; Orpo says pandemic risk low but response ready",
      "summary": "Prime Minister Orpo announced the government was ready to convene an emergency session from Monday 11 May to classify the Andes-type hantavirus as a dangerous contagious disease, after two Finns were identified as potentially exposed on a cruise ship. THL confirmed two individuals had not yet been tested; Orpo said the pandemic risk was assessed as small."
    },
    {
      "headline": "PM Orpo delivers EU policy speech calling for a stronger, geopolitically capable Europe",
      "summary": "PM Orpo delivered Finland's EU policy address at Aalto University on 8 May, arguing Europe must develop economic, defence and foreign policy strength, warning that values without power cannot be defended. Orpo referenced Russia's war in Ukraine and shifting US engagement, and announced Finland would host a European Arctic Summit in autumn 2026."
    },
    {
      "headline": "German President Steinmeier makes state visit to Helsinki; Stubb praises Germany's defence build-up",
      "summary": "German Federal President Frank-Walter Steinmeier visited Helsinki on 7 May 2026, meeting President Stubb and PM Orpo. Stubb praised Germany's expanding military as strengthening the whole of Europe, and said the US is not withdrawing from Europe but shifting the burden. The pair also visited a civilian bomb shelter in Helsinki."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Stubb visits Czech Republic; lenkkidiplomatia coverage and Nato/US comments draw attention",
