    },
    {
      "headline": "Orpo at EPC summit in Yerevan: Finland assesses Ukraine drone cooperation and Ukraine EU membership",
      "summary": "PM Orpo represented Finland at the 8th European Political Community summit in Yerevan, Armenia on 4 May, attending a Ukraine support meeting with Zelensky, Starmer, Macron and others. Orpo chaired a connectivity working group, discussed Ukraine sanctions, drone cooperation and potential EU membership, and said there is no reason to delay a possible Finland-Ukraine drone deal."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bank of Finland publishes China economy forecast; board visits US Federal Reserve",
      "summary": "The Bank of Finland's Institute for Emerging Economies (BOFIT) forecast China's real GDP growth at around 4% in 2026, supported by exports while domestic consumption remains weak. The Bank of Finland's supervisory board also made a visit to the US Federal Reserve and IMF in Washington DC and New York on 3-8 May. A separate household savings dashboard was also launched."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Survey: 77% of Finns support EU reducing economic dependency on US and China",
      "summary": "A joint survey by Finnish think-tanks Sitra and EVA found that 77% of Finns support the EU reducing economic and technological dependency on the US and China, even if this affects bilateral ties. Researchers noted this reflected strategic concern rather than direct anti-Americanism."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Putin makes threatening statements about Finland and Karelia; analysts assess Victory Day messaging",
      "summary": "Russian President Putin publicly stated that Finland wants to 'seize back' territories lost in the Winter and Continuation Wars, a claim Finnish analysts said represents an escalation in rhetoric. Putin's Victory Day parade on 9 May was notably smaller than previous years, with no missile systems displayed, which Western analysts interpreted as signalling weakness."
    },
    {
      "headline": "SUPO chief calls for public debate on Finnish intelligence culture and capabilities",
      "summary": "SUPO (Finnish Security Intelligence Service) Director Juha Martelius gave a public interview arguing Finland lacks a sufficiently developed intelligence culture, and that public debate about what kind of intelligence capabilities Finland wants is overdue. Martelius had written in SUPO's March national security review that strong intelligence capability is a key national asset."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Orpo elderly care comments; court system funding concerns; 2027 election candidate nominations",
